{%- comment -%}
  zv-woning-koop-lines (2026-11-03): prints the variant id of each KOOP Woning line that is IN THE
  CART, pipe-separated and in the same order as `handles` (zv_woning_koop_handles, so entry i is
  the one-time Woning line of the product at index i of zv_woning_handles). 0 where the cart has
  no such line, which keeps the list parallel and never matches a cart line.

  Unlike zv-woning-variants this does NOT look anything up with all_products: the Oplossingen
  page, the header's zv-hidden-cart-lines and /cart already resolve 20 unique handles (Shopify's
  limit per page), so two more would come back blank. A line is recognised from the cart itself,
  by its product handle AND its first variant's SKU being the config's (the same pair check as for
  every other product); the id is the line's own. That is all the server-side readers need (hide
  it from the item count, label it, gate it). Adding the line when it is missing needs an id the
  cart doesn't have yet: the scripts fetch /products/<handle>.js for that (zv-cart-guard rule 5,
  oplossingen.liquid's woningKoopLinePlan()).

  Params (render scope can't see the caller's zv_* variables, so pass them in; `cart` is global):
    handles - zv_woning_koop_handles
    skus    - zv_woning_koop_skus
  Usage: capture it, then `| strip`, and `| split: '|'` for a list of strings.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign wk_handles = handles | split: '|'
  assign wk_skus = skus | split: '|'
  assign wk_out = ''
  for h in wk_handles
    assign wk_id = 0
    for item in cart.items
      if wk_id == 0 and item.product.handle == h and item.sku == wk_skus[forloop.parentloop.index0]
        assign wk_id = item.variant_id
      endif
    endfor
    if forloop.first
      assign wk_out = wk_id | append: ''
    else
      assign wk_out = wk_out | append: '|' | append: wk_id
    endif
  endfor
  echo wk_out
-%}
